posting: raw BEGIN/COMMIT as nested transactions; dialog theme background; sheets that slide in

Three runtime gaps that kept Instagram from publishing and from showing its bottom sheets:

1. SQLiteStatement: AOSP SQLiteSession.executeSpecial turns a raw BEGIN / COMMIT /
   END / ROLLBACK (not ROLLBACK TO) into the nested transaction API. Sent to
   sqlite, a BEGIN inside SQLiteOpenHelper's onCreate transaction failed, so
   Instagram's pending-media store never opened: a rendered post was never
   committed and Share did nothing. Measured: posts with caption and music now
   publish.
2. Dialog: the window background is the dialog THEME's windowBackground (from
   its own cascade); the AOSP default inset panel only when the theme declares
   none. Instagram's sheets declare a transparent one; the grey 16dp panel
   squeezed them.
3. WindowOverlayStack: a dialog window is measured/laid out only when it asked
   for layout or its frame changed (ViewRootImpl), and its tree observer gets
   OnGlobalLayout after layout and OnPreDraw before draw. Re-laying it out on
   every draw restarted a sheet's slide-in each frame; the never-dispatched
   global layout left sheets that wait for it below the screen.
Diagnostics: the view dump includes dialog windows; MACAPK_TRACE_ENTRY_MAX.

